INT. COURTROOM 4B - POWER OUTAGE - DAY

Emergency lights bleed amber across empty benches. The air conditioner has died with a wheeze. The judge's bench looms.

ADVOCATE LEONARD OSEI-BANKS (50s, double-breasted suit) stands at the defense table. PROSECUTOR NADINE TOLLIVER-REEVES (40s, sleek braid) stands at hers. The judge's bench is a dark shape; only a voice comes from it.

LEONARD
Your Honor, with the lights out, I move to adjourn.

NADINE
Your Honor, the State opposes.

JUDGE FAIRCHILD (V.O.)
(over bench intercom)
Order! Counsel, I can hear you perfectly well.

LEONARD
Your Honor, I cannot see my client.

NADINE
^Your Honor, he can see his client perfectly.

LEONARD
(overlapping)
I do not...

NADINE
(overlapping)
...he has been looking at him for ten minutes...

JUDGE FAIRCHILD (V.O.)
(over both)
Quiet!

JUDGE FAIRCHILD (V.O.)
(over bench intercom, crackling)
Building says generators in five minutes. We will wait.

Leonard lowers his hand. Nadine folds her arms.

LEONARD
Your Honor, may I use the time to confer with my client?

JUDGE FAIRCHILD (V.O.)
By all means.

NADINE
Your Honor, with respect, the client has no idea where we are.

LEONARD
(to Nadine)
Miss Tolliver-Reeves, none of us do.

The emergency lights flicker. Then, all at once, the courtroom blazes with full, merciless brightness.
